    "text": "Yes. The Pine Street apartment has a monthly rent of 650 pounds. The Cedar Street one costs 690.\n\nPine has the bigger bedroom, but the kitchen is smaller than Cedar's. The bathroom is private in both places.\n\nYes, a sofa and a small table. I checked the floor and took a picture of a stain on the ceiling. The wall is a pale color. There was no leak near the window when I visited.\n\nHeating uses electricity. The electricity charge is included in the rent, and there is no gas supply in that apartment.\n\nThe draft contract lists a deposit of 300 pounds and a six-month lease. I want to read the agreement carefully and ask about any existing damage before I sign.\n\nThe ceiling is lower, but the window in the living room is larger. It is as quiet as Pine in the afternoon. The front door looks secure, though I will check it again.\n\nThe suggested date is Saturday. I have the address written here. First, I will ask whether the landlord can repair a loose cupboard door.\n\nNo. I can take the information home and compare the rooms, any other bill and the travel time before replying.",
